Frontend (Web & Mobile)
Category	Technology Stack	Rationale
Development Language	JavaScript / TypeScript	Single language for maximum code reuse across web and mobile.
Web Host / Micro-Frontends	ReactJS, Web Components (Custom Elements)	Modern, component-based UI; Strong encapsulation and interoperability for micro-frontends.
Mobile Host / Micro-Apps	React Native (with Hermes & New Architecture)	Native UX/performance on iOS/Android; Addresses past performance concerns; Unified developer experience.
Micro-Frontend Orchestration	Module Federation (Webpack 5 / Rspack)	Enables dynamic runtime code sharing, dependency deduplication, and independent deployment of features.
Mobile Module Bundling	Re.Pack	Replaces Metro to bring Webpack 5's Module Federation capabilities to React Native.
Shared Code	Monorepo Structure: platform-core & design-system packages	Maximizes reuse of business logic, API clients, state management, and design tokens across platforms.
Deployment & Ops	Zephyr Cloud (BYOC Model)	Dedicated platform for Module Federation; Provides instant rollbacks, versioning, and live environment composition within the bank's secure cloud.


Backend & Infrastructure
Category	Technology Stack	Rationale
Backend Framework	Spring Boot	Robust, widely adopted, and enterprise-grade framework for building scalable microservices.
API Architecture	RESTful APIs / Event-Driven (e.g., Kafka)	Standardized and scalable communication for microservices; Supports asynchronous event processing.
Containerization	Docker	Standard for packaging microservices for consistent deployment across environments.
Container Orchestration	Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform	Enterprise-grade Kubernetes platform for deploying, scaling, and managing backend microservices securely.
Database	(To be determined based on specific service needs, e.g., PostgreSQL, Oracle, MongoDB)	Flexible choice based on data consistency, performance, and scalability requirements for each microservice.
CI/CD	GitLab CI/CD (or equivalent)	Automates build, test, and deployment pipelines across frontend and backend, integrating with Zephyr Cloud and OpenShift.
Monitoring & Logging	Splunk, Dynatrace, Tealeaf	Enterprise-grade solutions for centralized logging, application performance monitoring (APM), and user experience analytics.


